<%# locals: (roster:, required_signatures:, **) %>
<%#
  SIGNER ROSTER — one row per wallet that can sign this treasury action, in
  the order given, which IS the signing order.

  DRIVEN FROM cosign.js, NOT FROM ALPINE. Each row exposes
  data-signer-row="<base58>", and the indicator inside it exposes
  data-signer-state. The JS writes one of pending / connected / signing /
  signed / failed into data-state on that indicator. All five are styled
  here, so a state the CSS does not know about cannot render as a blank
  circle that reads like "pending".

  DO NOT NUMBER THESE ROWS. It is tempting, because cosign.js already says
  "(2 of 3)" in its status line — but that count comes from signerQueue,
  which is [cosigner] + extras and does NOT contain the server row. Roster
  position and prompt position therefore disagree by one on every row below
  the server, and a number here would quietly contradict the status line the
  operator is reading at the same moment.

  THE SERVER ROW IS NOT PRE-CHECKED. It carries an Auto chip and says it
  signs by itself, which is what makes it "not your job" — but its indicator
  still starts at pending, because at render time the server has not signed
  anything yet. A green check standing for a signature that does not exist is
  the same lie as an Execute button at 2 of 3: it reads as progress and it is
  not. Flip the default here only if the server signature genuinely exists
  before this renders.
%>
<%# WHO HOLDS EACH WALLET — OPTIONAL, AND ABSENT MEANS ABSENT.

    /admin/authorities passes a resolved {address => User} map; the treasury
    console does not, and must keep rendering exactly as it did. So this reads
    through `local_assigns` with an empty default rather than through a declared
    local: an un-passed local would raise here, and a `defined?` check in a
    partial is the wrong instrument (see the block_given? trap — a partial
    inherits the layout's frame, so "is it there" questions want local_assigns).

    NO AVATAR IN THIS LIST, DELIBERATELY. Every row already leads with the
    signing-state indicator cosign.js drives, and a second circle beside it
    reads as a second status rather than as a face. The name and the wallet kind
    carry the identity here; the avatars live on the planner and the armed diff,
    where no indicator competes with them. %>
<% identities = local_assigns.fetch(:identities, {}) %>
<% fee_payer_row  = roster.find { |signer| signer[:fee_payer] } %>
<% fee_unfunded   = fee_payer_row.present? && fee_payer_row[:funded] == false %>
<% blocked_reason = fee_unfunded ? "The fee payer holds no SOL, so this transaction cannot pay its network fee." : "" %>

<section data-signer-roster
         data-required-signatures="<%= required_signatures %>"
         data-signer-roster-blocked="<%= fee_unfunded ? "true" : "false" %>"
         data-signer-blocked-reason="<%= blocked_reason %>"
         class="w-full rounded-lg border border-subtle bg-surface-alt p-2.5">

  <h3 class="label-upper text-3xs text-muted">Signing roster</h3>
  <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-heading">
    <%= pluralize(required_signatures, "signature") %> required
  </p>
  <p class="mt-0.5 text-3xs text-muted">Signed in the order shown.</p>

  <ol class="mt-2 space-y-1.5">
    <% roster.each do |signer| %>
      <% address    = signer[:address].to_s %>
      <% short      = address.length > 9 ? "#{address[0, 4]}…#{address[-4, 4]}" : address %>
      <% row_blocks = signer[:fee_payer] && signer[:funded] == false %>
      <li data-signer-row="<%= address %>"
          data-signer-role="<%= signer[:role] %>"
          class="flex items-start gap-2 rounded-md border px-2 py-1.5
                 <%= row_blocks ? "border-danger bg-danger/10" : "border-subtle bg-surface" %>">

        <%# THE INDICATOR. data-state is the only thing the JS touches; the
            glyph and the colour both follow from it, and the matching word is
            carried in an sr-only span so a screen reader tracks the same
            change without the JS having to maintain a label.

            THE IN-FLIGHT STATES ARE VIOLET, NOT PRIMARY, and that is not a
            taste call. This app's primary IS its success green (both resolve
            from #2E7D32 since 2026-09-16, and both resolved from #4BAF50
            before), so connected, signing and signed all came out the same
            hue — measured in a browser, in both themes, before this
            changed. Green means DONE and
            nothing else, which is the whole point of the check. Violet is a
            real brand colour here, safelisted in config/tailwind.config.js,
            and it takes the darker 600 on light surfaces and the base on dark
            ones because neither single shade clears 3 to 1 against both. %>
        <span data-signer-state
              data-state="pending"
              class="group/state relative mt-0.5 flex h-4 w-4 shrink-0 items-center justify-center
                     rounded-full border text-3xs font-bold leading-none
                     data-[state=pending]:border-strong data-[state=pending]:text-muted
                     data-[state=connected]:border-violet-600 data-[state=connected]:text-violet-600
                     data-[state=connected]:ring-2 data-[state=connected]:ring-violet-600/30
                     dark:data-[state=connected]:border-violet dark:data-[state=connected]:text-violet
                     dark:data-[state=connected]:ring-violet/30
                     data-[state=signing]:border-violet-600/40 data-[state=signing]:text-violet-600
                     dark:data-[state=signing]:border-violet/40 dark:data-[state=signing]:text-violet
                     data-[state=signed]:border-success data-[state=signed]:bg-success/15 data-[state=signed]:text-success-ink
                     data-[state=failed]:border-danger data-[state=failed]:bg-danger/15 data-[state=failed]:text-danger-ink">
          <span class="hidden group-data-[state=pending]/state:block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-current opacity-60"></span>
          <span class="sr-only hidden group-data-[state=pending]/state:inline">Not signed yet</span>

          <span class="hidden group-data-[state=connected]/state:block h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-current"></span>
          <span class="sr-only hidden group-data-[state=connected]/state:inline">Selected in Phantom</span>

          <span class="hidden group-data-[state=signing]/state:block h-3 w-3 animate-spin rounded-full
                       border-2 border-transparent border-t-current motion-reduce:animate-none"></span>
          <span class="sr-only hidden group-data-[state=signing]/state:inline">Signing</span>

          <span aria-hidden="true" class="hidden group-data-[state=signed]/state:block">&check;</span>
          <span class="sr-only hidden group-data-[state=signed]/state:inline">Signed</span>

          <span aria-hidden="true" class="hidden group-data-[state=failed]/state:block">&times;</span>
          <span class="sr-only hidden group-data-[state=failed]/state:inline">Failed</span>
        </span>

        <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-1.5 gap-y-0.5">
            <%# data-signer-address is the JS hook for a live repoint: the
                operator can change the extra-wallet select after this rendered,
                and a roster still naming the old wallet would be lying about
                which account he is about to be asked to switch to — which is
                the one thing he reads this row for. %>
            <span data-signer-address
                  class="font-mono text-2xs text-heading" title="<%= address %>"><%= short %></span>
            <% if signer[:signs_automatically] %>
              <span class="rounded bg-surface-alt px-1 py-px text-3xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">Auto</span>
            <% end %>
          </div>

          <p class="text-3xs text-secondary"><%= signer[:label] %></p>

          <%# THE HOLDER, WHEN THE CALLER RESOLVED ONE. A miss says so rather
              than printing nothing: on a roster the operator reads to decide
              which wallet to open, a silent blank is indistinguishable from a
              name that failed to render. %>
          <% if identities.present? %>
            <% holder = identities[address] %>
            <p class="mt-0.5 text-3xs <%= holder ? "font-bold text-heading" : "text-muted" %>">
              <%= holder ? holder.display_name : "No linked account" %>
              <span class="font-normal text-muted">
                <%= holder ? (holder.web3_solana_address == address ? "· Phantom" : "· Managed") : "· unresolved" %>
              </span>
            </p>
          <% end %>

          <% if signer[:signs_automatically] %>
            <p class="mt-0.5 text-3xs text-muted">Signs on the server. Nothing for you to do.</p>
          <% end %>

          <%# THE FEE PAYER'S BALANCE. Shown at 4 decimal places because that is
              the precision the caller supplies; a nil balance says so in words
              rather than rendering a zero it was never given. %>
          <% if signer[:fee_payer] %>
            <% if signer[:balance_sol].nil? %>
              <p class="mt-0.5 text-3xs text-warning-ink">Balance could not be read.</p>
            <% else %>
              <p class="mt-0.5 font-mono text-3xs <%= row_blocks ? "text-danger-ink" : "text-secondary" %>">
                <%= number_with_precision(signer[:balance_sol], precision: 4) %> SOL
              </p>
            <% end %>

            <% if row_blocks %>
              <p class="mt-1 text-3xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-danger-ink">Blocked</p>
              <p class="text-3xs text-danger-ink">
                This account pays the network fee and it is empty. Fund it before
                you sign.
              </p>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ol>

  <%# The cosigners are not fee payers. Account 0 is the server's admin key, so
      a cosigning wallet with a zero balance is FINE, and saying so here stops
      an operator funding a wallet that never needed it. %>
  <p class="mt-2 border-t border-subtle pt-2 text-3xs text-muted">
    Only the fee payer needs SOL. The cosigning wallets pay nothing, so a zero
    balance on one of them is fine.
  </p>
</section>
